<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Hand-encoded from the crop at loc_maple_leaf_p3_trio_seconds_chord.png: one
measure of the Maple Leaf Rag trio (Library of Congress scan,
musihas-200033264, page 3, public domain), its right hand repeating a
seconds-apart A5b/A4b/D4b figure and its left hand a four-note chord
(A3b, B3 natural, F3 natural, D3 natural: the natural signs are printed,
cancelling the 4-flat key signature on D and B only) whose top two notes
and whose bottom two notes are each a second apart: the shape heads.py's
_split_wide_cluster exists for (see AGENTS.md's heads.py bullet). Pitches
were read off the crop (staff position, then the printed accidentals) and
cross-checked against the piece's own MusicXML (music21 corpus,
joplin/maple_leaf_rag.mxl); grace notes are present in the source but
omitted here (a small/grace head with no matching grace note in the
MusicXML is dropped, not counted as a miss: see align.head_match.
Rhythm is a placeholder (uniform eighths, left to right): only each
note's measure, staff and staff position, and its left-to-right order
among repeats at that position, are asserted by test_geometry.py.
-->
